      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence directly supports an answer. The Discussion section states the third important finding: corpora miss some census languages, but \"in this case Twitter has fewer missing languages.\" The authors explain that Twitter provides a better representation of North America and Oceania and that Twitter's population match is better when weighted by GDP (worse by internet-usage), implying Twitter represents wealthier/urban populations; also many countries with English/Spanish mainly will be well represented on Twitter. These are the authors' offered explanations/hypotheses for why Twitter better predicts the language inventory."
      },
